<body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="topbar"><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="#home" aria-label="Nishith — home">N<span>.</span></a><nav class="links" id="navlinks" aria-label="Primary"><a href="#about">About</a><a href="#capabilities">Capabilities</a><a href="#skills">Skills</a><a href="#projects">Projects</a><a href="#journey">Experience</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav><div class="actions"><button class="iconbtn" id="themeBtn" aria-label="Switch to light theme" aria-pressed="false">☼</button><button class="menuBtn" id="menuBtn" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navlinks">☰</button></div></div></header>
<main id="main">
<section class="wrap hero" id="home"><div><div class="eyebrow">Data Engineering · Data Intelligence · AI</div><h1>Turning data into <span class="gradient">decisions</span><br>and ideas into systems.</h1><p class="lead">I'm Nishith — a data engineering professional expanding into machine learning and generative AI. I work across data pipelines, data quality, analytics and intelligent applications.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href="#projects">Explore projects ↗</a><a class="btn" href="#contact">Get in touch</a></div></div><aside class="hero-card" aria-label="Profile summary"><div class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">N</div><h3>Nishith</h3><p>Data Engineer · Data + AI Practitioner</p><div class="statgrid"><div class="stat"><b>5 yrs</b><small>Data engineering experience</small></div><div class="stat"><b>6</b><small>Capability areas</small></div><div class="stat"><b>ML</b><small>Modeling &amp; evaluation</small></div><div class="stat"><b>GenAI</b><small>LLMs &amp; AI agents</small></div></div></aside></section>
<section class="section" id="about"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">01 / About</div><h2>Data foundations.<br>Intelligent applications.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">A profile at the intersection of enterprise data engineering and emerging AI technologies — grounded in practical data workflows.</p></div><div class="about"><div class="panel"><h3>Professional profile</h3><p>Data engineering professional with experience in ETL development, data warehousing, SQL, production support and data modernization. Familiar with IBM DataStage, Teradata, Unix and Spark-based processing concepts, with growing focus on machine learning, LLM applications and cloud-native AI.</p><p>I enjoy taking a problem from raw data through preparation, analysis and automation — and making the result understandable to the people who use it.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>What I bring</h3><ul class="bullets"><li>ETL development, transformation logic and production troubleshooting.</li><li>Data cleansing, profiling, validation and reconciliation workflows.</li><li>SQL and Python-based analysis and data preparation.</li><li>ML problem framing, algorithm selection and model evaluation.</li><li>Exploration of RAG, Gemini, Vertex AI and AI agent patterns.</li><li>Product thinking: translating recurring workflows into useful tools.</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="capabilities"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">02 / Capabilities</div><h2>From raw records<br>to useful intelligence.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">An end-to-end view of the data lifecycle, with AI and ML as additional layers rather than replacements for sound data engineering.</p></div><div class="grid" id="capabilityGrid"></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="skills"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">03 / Technology</div><h2>Tools &amp; technologies</h2></div><p class="section-intro">Depth varies by tool. The marker on each group shows my current level so nothing is overstated.</p></div><div class="legend" aria-label="Proficiency legend"><span><i class="dot hands-on" aria-hidden="true"></i> Hands-on</span><span><i class="dot working" aria-hidden="true"></i> Working knowledge</span><span><i class="dot learning" aria-hidden="true"></i> Currently learning</span></div><div class="skillgrid" id="skillGrid"></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="projects"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">04 / Selected work</div><h2>Projects &amp; product explorations</h2></div><p class="section-intro">A mix of technical project directions and independent product concepts. Status labels are explicit so concepts are not mistaken for shipped products.</p></div><div class="project-toolbar" id="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects"><button class="filter" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button><button class="filter" data-filter="data" aria-pressed="false">Data &amp; ML</button><button class="filter" data-filter="ai" aria-pressed="false">AI products</button><button class="filter" data-filter="apps" aria-pressed="false">Applications</button></div><p class="result-count" id="resultCount" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="grid" id="projectGrid"></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="journey"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">05 / Experience</div><h2>Professional journey</h2></div><p class="section-intro">A capability-led summary of my experience so far.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="timeline"><div class="event"><h3>Enterprise Data Engineering</h3><p>DataStage development and support, parallel and sequencer jobs, Teradata SQL, ETL transformations, data loading and production troubleshooting.</p></div><div class="event"><h3>Data modernization &amp; Spark</h3><p>Exposure to migration patterns from traditional warehouse/ETL workloads toward Spark, Parquet and Delta Lake processing.</p></div><div class="event"><h3>Cloud &amp; AI expansion</h3><p>Learning and project exploration across GCP, BigQuery, Vertex AI, Gemini, RAG, LLM applications and AI agents.</p></div><div class="event"><h3>Independent product building</h3><p>Defining practical SaaS ideas and technical architectures across DataOps, analytics, productivity and workflow automation.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="contact"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">06 / Contact</div><h2>Let's build something<br>useful with data.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">Interested in Data Engineering, Data + AI opportunities, technical collaboration or building practical AI products.</p></div><div class="contact"><div><h3>Open to conversations</h3><p class="muted">The form opens your email app with the message pre-filled — nothing is sent to a server. You can also copy my email address directly.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Data Engineering</span><span class="tag">Data + AI</span><span class="tag">Machine Learning</span><span class="tag">Generative AI</span></div><div class="social-row" id="socialRow"></div></div><form class="contactbox" id="contactForm" novalidate><h3>Send a message</h3><label for="visitor">Your name</label><input id="visitor" name="visitor" autocomplete="name" required placeholder="Your name"><label for="email">Your email</label><input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required placeholder="you@example.com"><label for="message">Message</label><textarea id="message" name="message" required placeholder="Tell me what you'd like to discuss..."></textarea><button class="btn primary" type="submit" style="margin-top:14px">Create email ↗</button> <button class="btn" type="button" id="copyEmailBtn" style="margin-top:14px">Copy my email</button><p class="form-msg" id="formMsg" aria-live="polite"></p></form></div></div></section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap footer"><span>© <span id="year"></span> Nishith. Built with curiosity and data.</span><span>Data Engineering · Analytics · ML · Generative AI · <a href="#home">Back to top ↑</a></span></footer>
<div class="modal" id="modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="modalTitle" hidden><div class="modalbox"><button class="iconbtn close" id="closeModal" aria-label="Close project brief">✕</button><div class="kicker">Project brief</div><h2 id="modalTitle"></h2><p id="modalDesc" class="muted"></p></div></div>
<noscript><p style="padding:20px;text-align:center">This portfolio uses JavaScript for project filtering and the contact form. Please enable JavaScript to use those features.</p></noscript>
<script>
"use strict";
const CONFIG = { email: "", linkedin: "", github: "", resumeUrl: "" };
const CAPABILITIES = [
  {n:"01 — ENGINEERING",t:"Data Engineering",d:"Build and support reliable data movement and transformation workflows across batch processing and warehouse environments.",tags:["ETL","DataStage","Teradata","PySpark"]},
  {n:"02 — QUALITY",t:"Data Cleansing & Quality",d:"Profile datasets, identify duplicates and missing values, standardize fields, validate rules and reconcile source-to-target results.",tags:["Profiling","Deduplication","Validation","Reconciliation"]},
  {n:"03 — TEST DATA",t:"Synthetic Data Generation",d:"Create configurable mock datasets for development, testing and demonstrations, including controlled nulls, duplicates and edge cases.",tags:["CSV","JSON","Parquet","Test scenarios"]},
  {n:"04 — ANALYTICS",t:"Data Analysis & EDA",d:"Explore distributions, trends, correlations and data quality patterns; communicate findings with clear charts and reports.",tags:["SQL","Pandas","Statistics","Visualization"]},
  {n:"05 — MODELING",t:"Machine Learning",d:"Frame supervised and unsupervised learning problems, prepare features, compare models and evaluate performance with appropriate metrics.",tags:["Classification","Regression","Clustering","Anomaly detection"]},
  {n:"06 — GENERATIVE AI",t:"Generative AI & Agents",d:"Explore LLM-powered workflows for querying data, explaining pipeline issues, retrieving knowledge and automating repeatable tasks.",tags:["Gemini","Vertex AI","RAG","AI agents"]}
];
const SKILLS = [
  {t:"Data Engineering",level:"hands-on",d:"IBM DataStage 11.3–11.7 · ETL · CDC · Sequencer & Parallel jobs"},
  {t:"Databases & SQL",level:"hands-on",d:"Teradata · SQL · BTEQ · FastLoad · MultiLoad · TPT"},
  {t:"Big Data",level:"working",d:"PySpark · Spark SQL · Parquet · Delta Lake"},
  {t:"Cloud & Platforms",level:"working",d:"GCP · BigQuery · Cloud Storage · Databricks"},
  {t:"Programming",level:"hands-on",d:"Python · Unix shell · Git"},
  {t:"DevOps & Scheduling",level:"working",d:"GitHub · Jenkins · CI/CD · Control-M"},
  {t:"Machine Learning",level:"learning",d:"Scikit-learn concepts · model evaluation · feature preparation"},
  {t:"Generative AI",level:"learning",d:"Gemini · Vertex AI · LLMs · RAG · embeddings · agents"}
];
const PROJECTS = [
  {cat:"data",status:"Flagship concept · Proposed",t:"DataPilot ML Studio",d:"A unified workbench concept: upload datasets, profile and clean data, run EDA, recommend ML approaches, compare models and generate reports.",tags:["Python","Pandas","Scikit-learn","FastAPI","Next.js"],brief:"Proposed flagship portfolio build. Planned flow: ingest CSV/Excel/JSON/Parquet; profile and cleanse; run EDA; recommend supervised or unsupervised algorithms based on target and objective; compare models using suitable metrics; export predictions and HTML/PDF reports. Suggested stack: Python, Pandas, Scikit-learn, XGBoost, FastAPI, Next.js and MLflow. Not yet a completed deployed product."},
  {cat:"data",status:"Capability / project direction",t:"Data Cleansing Assistant",d:"Automate dataset profiling, null and duplicate detection, standardization, validation rules and quality summaries.",tags:["Python","Pandas","Data quality"],brief:"Project direction: ingest a dataset, generate a quality profile, flag missing and duplicate values, detect suspicious ranges and inconsistent formats, propose transformations, preserve an audit log and export a cleaned dataset. Cleaning actions should be reviewable rather than silently destructive."},
  {cat:"data",status:"Capability / project direction",t:"MockData Generator",d:"Generate realistic synthetic datasets with configurable schemas, row counts, distributions and deliberate edge cases for testing.",tags:["Python","CSV","JSON","Parquet"],brief:"Project direction: configure fields, data types, value ranges, relationships and distributions; generate sample customer, transaction or operational data; optionally inject nulls, duplicates and invalid values; export to CSV, JSON or Parquet. Synthetic data should not reproduce real personal records."},
  {cat:"data",status:"Capability / project direction",t:"Smart Data Analyzer",d:"Perform exploratory data analysis with summary statistics, correlations, trend views and downloadable reports.",tags:["SQL","Pandas","Plotly","EDA"],brief:"Project direction: infer column types, calculate descriptive statistics, visualize distributions, inspect correlations, identify outliers and create a reproducible HTML report with dataset caveats and methodology."},
  {cat:"data",status:"Product concept · Proposed",t:"AI Data Engineer Agent",d:"An assistant for understanding ETL logic, explaining failures, generating documentation and supporting migration analysis.",tags:["LLMs","ETL metadata","RAG","PySpark"],brief:"Product concept: parse job metadata and SQL, explain transformation logic, retrieve internal runbooks, summarize errors and draft migration code. Any generated code should be reviewed and tested against source/target outputs before use."},
  {cat:"ai",status:"Product concept / planning",t:"AI Intelligence Daily",d:"A curated intelligence product covering AI research, new tools, GitHub projects, startups and cloud technology.",tags:["LLMs","Research","Telegram","Email"],brief:"Discussed product scope: public audience; AI and LLMs, AI products, developer tools, startups and funding, Google Cloud and AWS, open-source projects, research papers and technology news. Planned delivery: web dashboard, email and Telegram. Implementation status should be updated as work progresses."},
  {cat:"ai",status:"Product concept / architecture exploration",t:"LifePilot AI / Kivorly",d:"An AI-assisted goal planning and personal productivity platform with a web-first architecture.",tags:["Next.js","Firebase","Firestore","AI"],brief:"Discussed architecture: Next.js frontend, Firebase Authentication and Firestore, with a website-first experience and hybrid dashboard. Verify current implementation before describing as launched."},
  {cat:"ai",status:"Product concept",t:"PixelPilot AI / DataOps",d:"A DataOps automation concept focused on AI-assisted operational workflows and data engineering tasks.",tags:["DataOps","Automation","AI agents"],brief:"Independent startup concept for DataOps AI and workflow automation. Potential scope includes data pipeline assistance, operational intelligence and workflow automation. Concept stage unless implementation is independently verified."},
  {cat:"apps",status:"Requirements / MVP planning",t:"HomeBite",d:"A shared household meal coordination app for meal availability, expenses, recipes, waste and guest tracking.",tags:["Web app","Firestore","Notifications"],brief:"Discussed requirements for a seven-person household: lunch and dinner, admin-managed cook access, notifications, expenses, recipes, food waste, guest tracking and WhatsApp support. Status: product requirements and MVP planning."},
  {cat:"apps",status:"MVP specification",t:"Offline Poker Money Tracker",d:"A companion tracker for in-person poker games: buy-ins, rebuys, pot totals and winner settlement.",tags:["Web app","Ledger","Settlement logic"],brief:"Discussed MVP: physical/offline poker games only; players contribute buy-ins, multiple rebuys are supported, and the winner receives the pot. The app tracks money and settlement rather than hosting online poker gameplay."},
  {cat:"ai",status:"Product concept",t:"PixelPilot Health",d:"An AI patient companion concept for hospital communication through a website and WhatsApp.",tags:["Healthcare operations","AI assistant","WhatsApp"],brief:"Discussed concept: AI patient companion for hospitals, with a website and WhatsApp channel. Any real deployment would require clinical safety boundaries, privacy controls, security review and human escalation."}
];
const $ = (s, r=document) => r.querySelector(s);
const $$ = (s, r=document) => [...r.querySelectorAll(s)];
const esc = s => String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g, c => ({"&":"&amp;","<":"&lt;",">":"&gt;",'"':"&quot;","'":"&#39;"}[c]));
$("#capabilityGrid").innerHTML = CAPABILITIES.map(c => `<article class="card"><div class="num">${esc(c.n)}</div><h3>${esc(c.t)}</h3><p>${esc(c.d)}</p><div class="tags">${c.tags.map(t=>`<span class="tag">${esc(t)}</span>`).join("")}</div></article>`).join("");
const LEVEL_LABEL = {"hands-on":"Hands-on","working":"Working knowledge","learning":"Currently learning"};
$("#skillGrid").innerHTML = SKILLS.map(s => `<div class="skill"><strong><i class="dot ${esc(s.level)}" aria-hidden="true"></i>${esc(s.t)}</strong><span>${esc(s.d)}</span></div>`).join("");
$("#projectGrid").innerHTML = PROJECTS.map((p,i) => `<article class="card project" data-category="${esc(p.cat)}"><div class="status">${esc(p.status)}</div><h3>${esc(p.t)}</h3><p>${esc(p.d)}</p><div class="tags">${p.tags.map(t=>`<span class="tag">${esc(t)}</span>`).join("")}</div><div class="details"><button class="textlink" type="button" data-project="${i}" aria-haspopup="dialog">View project brief ↗</button></div></article>`).join("");
(function(){ const links=[]; if(CONFIG.linkedin)links.push(`<a href="${esc(CONFIG.linkedin)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>`); if(CONFIG.github)links.push(`<a href="${esc(CONFIG.github)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>`); if(CONFIG.resumeUrl)links.push(`<a href="${esc(CONFIG.resumeUrl)}" download>Download résumé ↓</a>`); $("#socialRow").innerHTML=links.join(""); })();
const themeBtn = $("#themeBtn");
function syncThemeBtn(){ const light=document.documentElement.dataset.theme==="light"; themeBtn.textContent=light?"☾":"☼"; themeBtn.setAttribute("aria-label",light?"Switch to dark theme":"Switch to light theme"); themeBtn.setAttribute("aria-pressed",String(light)); }
themeBtn.addEventListener("click",()=>{ const next=document.documentElement.dataset.theme==="light"?"dark":"light"; document.documentElement.dataset.theme=next; try{localStorage.setItem("portfolio-theme",next);}catch(e){} syncThemeBtn(); });
syncThemeBtn();
const menuBtn=$("#menuBtn"),navlinks=$("#navlinks");
menuBtn.addEventListener("click",()=>{ const open=navlinks.classList.toggle("open"); menuBtn.setAttribute("aria-expanded",String(open)); menuBtn.setAttribute("aria-label",open?"Close menu":"Open menu"); });
$$("#navlinks a").forEach(a=>a.addEventListener("click",()=>{ navlinks.classList.remove("open"); menuBtn.setAttribute("aria-expanded","false"); }));
const resultCount=$("#resultCount");
function applyFilter(f){ let shown=0; $$(".project").forEach(p=>{ const show=f==="all"||p.dataset.category===f; p.hidden=!show; if(show)shown++; }); resultCount.textContent=`Showing ${shown} of ${PROJECTS.length} projects`; }
$$(".filter").forEach(btn=>btn.addEventListener("click",()=>{ $$(".filter").forEach(b=>b.setAttribute("aria-pressed","false")); btn.setAttribute("aria-pressed","true"); applyFilter(btn.dataset.filter); }));
applyFilter("all");
const modal=$("#modal"),closeBtn=$("#closeModal"); let lastFocus=null;
function openModal(i){ const p=PROJECTS[i]; $("#modalTitle").textContent=p.t; $("#modalDesc").textContent=p.brief; lastFocus=document.activeElement; modal.hidden=false; modal.classList.add("show"); document.body.style.overflow="hidden"; closeBtn.focus(); }
function closeModal(){ modal.classList.remove("show"); modal.hidden=true; document.body.style.overflow=""; if(lastFocus)lastFocus.focus(); }
$("#projectGrid").addEventListener("click",e=>{ const btn=e.target.closest("[data-project]"); if(btn)openModal(Number(btn.dataset.project)); });
closeBtn.addEventListener("click",closeModal);
modal.addEventListener("click",e=>{ if(e.target===modal)closeModal(); });
document.addEventListener("keydown",e=>{ if(modal.hidden)return; if(e.key==="Escape")closeModal(); if(e.key==="Tab"){ const f=$$("button,a[href],input,textarea",modal).filter(el=>!el.disabled); if(!f.length)return; const first=f[0],last=f[f.length-1]; if(e.shiftKey&&document.activeElement===first){e.preventDefault();last.focus();} else if(!e.shiftKey&&document.activeElement===last){e.preventDefault();first.focus();} } });
const formMsg=$("#formMsg");
function showMsg(t,k){ formMsg.textContent=t; formMsg.className="form-msg "+(k||""); }
$("#contactForm").addEventListener("submit",e=>{ e.preventDefault(); const name=$("#visitor").value.trim(),email=$("#email").value.trim(),msg=$("#message").value.trim(); if(!name||!email||!msg){showMsg("Please fill in your name, email and a message.","error");return;} if(!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)){showMsg("That email address doesn't look valid — please check it.","error");$("#email").focus();return;} if(!CONFIG.email){showMsg("Contact email isn't configured yet. Please add CONFIG.email in the code (see docs/CONTENT-CHECKLIST.md).","error");return;} const subject=encodeURIComponent("Portfolio enquiry from "+name); const body=encodeURIComponent(`Name: ${name}\nEmail: ${email}\n\n${msg}`); showMsg("Opening your email app…","ok"); location.href=`mailto:${CONFIG.email}?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`; });
$("#copyEmailBtn").addEventListener("click",async()=>{ if(!CONFIG.email){showMsg("Contact email isn't configured yet. Please add CONFIG.email in the code.","error");return;} try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(CONFIG.email);showMsg("Email copied: "+CONFIG.email,"ok");}catch(e){showMsg("Couldn't copy automatically — my email is "+CONFIG.email,"error");} });
const navMap=new Map($$(".links a").map(a=>[a.getAttribute("href").slice(1),a]));
const spy=new IntersectionObserver(entries=>{ entries.forEach(en=>{ if(en.isIntersecting){ navMap.forEach(a=>a.classList.remove("active")); const link=navMap.get(en.target.id); if(link)link.classList.add("active"); } }); },{rootMargin:"-40% 0px -55% 0px"});
$$("main section[id]").forEach(s=>spy.observe(s));
$("#year").textContent=new Date().getFullYear();
</script>
</body>
</html>
